This extension adds Horizon Forbidden West modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]HFW Mod Manager automatically installed.[/summary]

[b][color=#ffff00][size=3][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/horizonforbiddenwest/mods/137]HFW Mod Manager [/url]will be automatically installed. It is required to install the latest mods.[/size][/color][/b]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Save Game (Documents) mods with a ".dat" file install to the game's save folder.[/*]
[*]HFW Manager mods with a "modinfo.json" file and a ".core" or ".stream" file install to the "mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]Downloads and copies the HFW Mod Manager executable into the game folder. You will get a notification reminding you to run the tool on each deployment.[/*]
[*]Includes an automatic installer for saves that goes to your Horizon Forbidden West Documents folder.[/*]
[*][size=2][color=#f9cb9c][b]You can re-download/update HFW Mod Manager at any time using the button within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar. [/b][/color][/size][/*]
[/list]
[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Horizon Forbidden West mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Save Game Files:

Save files, deployed to the game's save folder.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by any file with the ".dat" extension.

  Installs to: the game's save folder

  Common mistakes:
    - Including an example save alongside a normal mod makes the archive install as a save.

========================================================================

HFW Manager Mod:

Recognised when the archive contains a "modinfo.json" file and a ".core" or ".stream" file.

  Installs to: "mods"

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives that contain a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with "ModuleConfig.xml") are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead, and none of the rules above apply.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]
